# --- Secrets: never commit ------------------------------------------------
# The IRIS licence key is supplied by the operator, not by this repository.
secrets/*
!secrets/.gitkeep
!secrets/README.md

# --- IRIS licence keys ------------------------------------------------------
# A licence key is InterSystems property, is tied to a customer, and is not ours
# to publish. secrets/* below already covers the mounted copy at
# secrets/iris.key; these patterns cover an operator-supplied original dropped
# anywhere in the tree, whatever it is named.
*.ISCkey
*.isckey
iris.key
YKE44*

# --- SSH keys for the deployment host --------------------------------------
# Operator-supplied private keys for reaching the lab machine. Same rule as
# every other credential in this project: documented in the reports where a
# tester needs it, never in source control.
*.pem
*_key
id_rsa
id_ed25519

# --- Bulk archives: product images, installation kits, report bundles ------
# No archive belongs in this repository: an image tarball or an installation kit
# is licensed product and this is not a distribution channel for it, and a report
# archive is a measurement rather than source. Operators do drop such files into
# the working tree - that is what the working tree is for - so they are ignored
# here rather than left to be caught by `make check` after a careless `git add`.
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.tar.zst
*.tar.bz2
*.tar.xz
*.zip
*.iso
*.7z

# --- Forge access tokens ----------------------------------------------------
# A GitHub personal access token (or any other forge credential) an operator
# keeps in the tree to push with. Same rule as every other credential here: it
# never reaches source control. Nothing in this rig reads one - `git push` takes
# it from the operator's own credential helper or askpass, never from a path
# inside the repository.
github-PAT.txt
*-PAT.txt
*.pat
*_token
*.token

# --- Resolved configuration (per-deployment, machine specific) -------------
.env
.env.resolved

# --- Downloaded / extracted third-party artefacts --------------------------
# FHIR packages are fetched at deploy time (make packages). They are large,
# licensed by their respective publishers, and fully reproducible from
# .env.resolved, so they are not tracked.
vendor/

# --- Rendered configuration -----------------------------------------------
# Generated from tiger/*.tmpl by scripts/30-render-config.sh
run/

# --- Rendered test data ----------------------------------------------------
# build/fhir/<level>/ is what scripts/lib/build_testdata.py renders from the
# authored sources in testdata/fhir/. It is derived twice over - from those
# sources and from vendor/requirements.json, which belongs to whichever test
# suite version this deployment pinned - so committing it would freeze one
# version's profile canonicals and resource IDs into the repository, where they
# would silently disagree with a run that pinned a different TESTSUITE_VERSION.
# The authored sources under testdata/fhir/ are tracked; this is not.
#
# generated/<suite-version>/ is the deliberate exception and does not contradict
# this: a copy under a path that NAMES the version it belongs to cannot be
# mistaken for the current render, which is the only objection above. It is read
# by nothing. See generated/testsuite-3.0.9/README.md.
build/

# --- Test results ----------------------------------------------------------
# Reports are evidence, not source. Archive them out-of-band if you need to
# keep them; `make clean` deliberately does not touch this directory.
reports/

# --- Build-time index ------------------------------------------------------
gap-analysis/index.json

# --- Generated documentation ------------------------------------------------
# docs/en/generated/ is derived from the feature files of whichever test suite
# version this deployment pinned (scripts/25-extract-requirements.sh, run by
# `make packages`). Committing it would freeze one version's requirement tables
# into the repository, where they would silently disagree with a run that pinned
# a different TESTSUITE_VERSION - and the test-data specification is the one
# document that must not be stale. Everything else under docs/ is authored and
# tracked.
docs/en/generated/*
!docs/en/generated/README.md

# --- Editor / OS noise -----------------------------------------------------
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- Local tooling state ---------------------------------------------------
# settings.local.json holds one operator's own tool permissions, which are a
# property of that workstation and not of this project.
.claude/settings.local.json
